# The voice-recognition role on an NVIDIA graphics card (host/Dockerfile with ACCELERATOR=gpu): sherpa-onnx 1.13.8's own CUDA 12
# build (the same runtime as the desktop's, with ONNX Runtime 1.28.2 and its CUDA provider inside the wheel; k2-fsa publishes it
# on Hugging Face, pinned here to a commit and SHA-256) and NVIDIA's CUDA 12 and cuDNN 9 libraries from PyPI. numpy is the only
# other module sherpa-onnx's Python binding needs. Regenerate the lock with:
#   uv pip compile workers/voice-recognition/host/requirements-cuda.in --generate-hashes --python-version 3.12 --python-platform x86_64-manylinux_2_28 -o workers/voice-recognition/host/requirements-cuda.lock
sherpa-onnx @ https://huggingface.co/csukuangfj2/sherpa-onnx-wheels/resolve/4de10716b1043c13380c79f3f12127a6c6429650/cuda/1.13.8/sherpa_onnx-1.13.8%2Bcuda12.cudnn9.onnxruntime1.28.2-cp312-cp312-linux_x86_64.whl
numpy==2.5.3
nvidia-cuda-runtime-cu12~=12.0
nvidia-cuda-nvrtc-cu12~=12.0
nvidia-cublas-cu12~=12.0
nvidia-cufft-cu12~=11.0
nvidia-curand-cu12~=10.0
nvidia-cudnn-cu12~=9.0
